From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 06:56:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Describe the camera for the
 boot loader

Give the J604 the J713's camera description (aurora-silicon/linux
8295d7f019): empty isp-firmware-text and isp-firmware-data placeholders,
the 20 MiB isp-heap window at 0x100_0000_0000, the ISP's memory-region
and its two sensor presets. The ISP and its DARTs stay disabled; the
boot loader fills the placeholders from this boot's ADT, sets
apple,platform-id from the ADT's sensor-type and enables them, or leaves
the camera disabled.

Values (MEASURED on J604 ADTs: 25G83 and 26B123 templates, RT27.2 and
four 25G83 runtime trees from 2026-11-05):
- isp, ispRtb and dart-isp match the J713 byte for byte apart from
  phandles and sensor-type (0x2e here, 0x17 in the J713 isp node), so
  t8132.dtsi's nodes apply unchanged;
- the runtime segment-ranges are __TEXT 0xca4000 at 0x100_0000_0000 and
  __DATA 0x748000 right above it, inside DRAM and the 20 MiB window.

The presets are the J713/J616s IMX958 configuration 5, with 720p as the
whole 1080p window scaled down (99ec97ea33). That the J604 has the same
12 MP Center Stage module is INFERENCE: the driver checks the index
against the firmware's count at the first stream, and its dynamic debug
names the sensor it finds.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-camera.dtsi     | 68 +++++++++++++++++++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts      |  6 ++
 2 files changed, 74 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-camera.dtsi

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-camera.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-camera.dtsi
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..7058e81fea
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-camera.dtsi
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+ OR MIT
+/*
+ * Apple MacBook Pro (14-inch, M4, 2024) FaceTime HD camera (ISP).
+ *
+ * The ISP and its three DARTs are described disabled in t8132.dtsi. The
+ * J604 ADT's isp, ispRtb and dart-isp nodes match the J713's byte for byte
+ * (reg, interrupts, remap streams, vm-size, dapf-instance-0) in the 25G83
+ * and 26B123 templates, except sensor-type: 0x2e on the J604, 0x17 in the
+ * J713 isp node.
+ *
+ * iBoot loads the ISP firmware outside the kernel's memory, at addresses
+ * that move with the boot firmware. The boot loader fills the placeholders
+ * below from this boot's ADT isp segment-ranges (reg, and iommu-addresses
+ * where the firmware runs them, from 0x100_0000_0000 on), sets
+ * apple,platform-id from the ADT isp node's sensor-type and then enables
+ * the ISP and its DARTs. If it cannot, the camera stays disabled and the
+ * boot goes on. On this J604 under the 25G83 boot firmware the two
+ * segments are 0xca4000 and 0x748000 bytes, which fit the 20 MiB heap
+ * window (lab runtime ADTs, 2026-11-05).
+ *
+ * Copyright The Asahi Linux Contributors
+ */
+
+/ {
+	reserved-memory {
+		/*
+		 * The driver checks that the coprocessor's reset vector is this
+		 * text before it starts the firmware.
+		 */
+		isp_fw_text: isp-firmware-text { };
+
+		isp_fw_data: isp-firmware-data { };
+
+		/* the firmware's 20 MiB main memory, the driver allocates above it */
+		isp_heap: isp-heap {
+			iommu-addresses = <&isp 0x100 0x0 0x0 0x1400000>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&isp {
+	memory-region = <&isp_fw_text>, <&isp_fw_data>, <&isp_heap>;
+	memory-region-names = "text", "data", "heap";
+
+	/*
+	 * The front camera: the 12 MP Center Stage camera of the J713 and the
+	 * J614/J616 (an IMX958, firmware configuration 5). That the J604 has
+	 * the same module is not measured yet: the driver checks the
+	 * configuration index against the firmware's count at the first
+	 * stream, and logs the sensor it finds with dynamic debug.
+	 */
+	sensor-presets {
+		/* 1920x1080 */
+		preset0 {
+			apple,config-index = <5>;
+			apple,input-size = <1920 2160>;
+			apple,output-size = <1920 1080>;
+			apple,crop = <0 0 1920 1080>;
+		};
+		/* 1280x720: the same window as 1920x1080, scaled down */
+		preset1 {
+			apple,config-index = <5>;
+			apple,input-size = <1920 2160>;
+			apple,output-size = <1280 720>;
+			apple,crop = <0 0 1920 1080>;
+		};
+	};
+};
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index df5a180944..9f24fd68f8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -657,6 +657,12 @@
  */
 #include "t8132-j604-display.dtsi"
 
+/*
+ * FaceTime HD camera: the boot loader hands the ISP firmware over and enables
+ * the ISP (see t8132-j604-camera.dtsi).
+ */
+#include "t8132-j604-camera.dtsi"
+
 /*
  * AOP (always-on processor) audio: the three microphones and the headphone
  * jack. The AOP needs the loader's handoff: m1n1 programs the AOP DART's
